# HRM System — Cursor AI Rules
# Stack: Java 17 + RMI + Swing + MySQL

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# 1. HARD STACK CONSTRAINTS (DO NOT BREAK)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────

- Language: Java 17+
- UI: Java Swing ONLY (NO JavaFX, NO web UI)
- Distributed: Java RMI ONLY (UnicastRemoteObject, Naming, LocateRegistry)
- Database: MySQL 8.x via JDBC only
- Connection Pool: HikariCP only
- Password Hashing: jBCrypt (BCrypt only)

DO NOT USE:
- Spring / Spring Boot / Hibernate / JPA
- JavaFX, REST APIs, WebSockets, gRPC
- Raw Thread usage in Swing (must use SwingWorker)
- Statement (SQL must always use PreparedStatement)
- Hardcoded credentials (must use config.properties)
- Any external architecture not listed above

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# 2. RMI + DISTRIBUTED RULES
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────

- All remote methods MUST be defined in a Remote interface
- All remote methods MUST declare `throws RemoteException`
- Server implementation MUST extend UnicastRemoteObject
- RMI calls may be concurrent → assume multi-threaded execution
- Use synchronization only when modifying shared state (e.g., leave balance)

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# 3. DATABASE RULES (STRICT)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────

- MUST use PreparedStatement only (NO string concatenation SQL)
- MUST use connection pool (HikariCP)
- MUST close ResultSet + Statement using try-with-resources
- NEVER create raw JDBC connections manually outside DatabaseManager
- All DB access must go through DatabaseManager

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# 4. SWING UI RULES (STRICT)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────

- ALL RMI calls MUST be inside SwingWorker
- NEVER call remote methods directly on Event Dispatch Thread (EDT)
- ALL UI updates must happen on EDT (SwingUtilities.invokeLater or done())
- Use JOptionPane for all user messages
- Use JTable + DefaultTableModel for list data
- Use JTabbedPane for dashboards
- Use GridBagLayout for forms

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# 5. SECURITY RULES (STRICT)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────

- Passwords MUST be hashed using BCrypt before storage
- Password verification MUST use BCrypt.checkpw()
- Enforce role-based access:
  - HR-only methods must check role before execution
- Never log or expose plaintext passwords

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# 6. CODE QUALITY RULES
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────

- All model classes must be POJOs only (no DB logic)
- All models must implement Serializable with serialVersionUID = 1L
- Use java.sql.Date for all date fields
- Keep client/server/common separation strictly respected
- No business logic inside Swing UI classes
- Server must never crash → all methods must use try-catch and return RemoteException on failure

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# 7. ERROR HANDLING RULES
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────

- ALL remote methods must handle exceptions internally
- NEVER expose stack traces to client users
- Client must show user-friendly error dialogs
- Handle RemoteException and connection failures gracefully

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# 8. ARCHITECTURE RULE (HIGH LEVEL)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────

Client (Swing UI)
   ↓ RMI 
Server (Business Logic + DB Access)
   ↓ JDBC
MySQL Database

Keep this separation strict. No shortcuts.

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# 9. ABSOLUTE RULE
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────

If unsure:
→ Prefer simplicity
→ Prefer safety
→ Prefer correctness over optimization